  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Capacity and Collaboration to Combat Trafficking in Saiga Horn in Kazakhstan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to counter the trafficking of wildlife products in Kazakhstan and specifically to conserve the Critically Endangered saiga antelope (Saiga tatarica tatarica) by addressing the impacts of poaching and the illegal trade in saiga horn and derivatives. Specific activities will include: (1) investigating and mapping saiga horn trade routes and establishing protocols for collation and sharing of such dynamic information between enforcement agencies; (2) promoting and improving the use and coordination of strategic, intelligence-led anti-poaching patrolling and sniffer dog deployment, resulting in more effective enforcement; (3) strengthening anti-poaching by introducing new approaches such as SMART and building practical wildlife crime investigation skills to create a stronger evidence base for prosecutions; (4) promoting advocacy in the judiciary for the prosecution of wildlife crime; and (5) promoting improved standards in the use of sniffer dogs to detect illegally trafficked saiga horn and other wildlife products and cooperation with nascent sniffer dog programs in two neighboring transit countries.</narrative>
  </description>
